  "designIntent": {
    "firstRead": "A low folded bonnet and one continuous flared maid garment, not Lucario plus stacked accessories.",
    "macroRules": [
      "No stacked horizontal cap slabs.",
      "No single rectangular apron board.",
      "No paired rectangular apron shields.",
      "No rigid folding-fan silhouette across the whole front.",
      "Build front cloth as overlapping upper, mid and lower tiers whose outer contour widens toward an irregular hem.",
      "Recover additional silhouette through side drape and rear tails rather than frontal bulk.",
      "Each neighboring cloth panel changes direction, overlap, depth or hem height.",
      "Keep both ears and the face visually open.",
      "Carry white/periwinkle cloth through head, torso, sleeves, hips, front and rear.",
      "Spend geometry on contour changes, not repeated identical blocks."
    ],
    "referenceTechniqueCarryover": [
      "Two-stage parented drape and edge hierarchy from the inspected Ruins Style technique study.",
      "Whole-body costume continuity and anatomy-following shells from the inspected Space Style technique study.",
      "Connected head/torso garment hierarchy and animation-parented overlays from the inspected Covert Style technique study."
    ],
    "iterationNote": "Run 5 exact Blockbench evidence reached pixelDifferenceRatio 0.1904 and silhouetteDeltaRatio 0.0314. The two-piece front remained board-like and the bonnet remained visually weak. This pass replaces both large front sheets with three overlapping cloth tiers per side, creates a broken hem rather than one straight rectangle, and strengthens the low bonnet with visible sloped crown lobes and a split front rim while preserving ear clearance."
  },
